WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.000
SPEAKER 1: Hello.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.630
This video shows the Coursera
setup steps, including

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:06.780
your account on Coursera,
steps to enroll students,

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.300
and how to monitor
students' learning progress.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.880
To access the Admin
console, sign into Coursera

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.320
with your credentials.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.090
Coursera provides
several dashboards

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.530
at different stages
of the program

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.840
to track the
progress of students.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.180
The Admin dashboard and
the Program Admin pages

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:25.330
show the data for your members,
learners, and completers.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.330
This sample data shows you
how students are progressing

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.009
through your learning programs.

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:37.150
A student's status may be
active, inactive, or at risk.

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:39.040
In the Invitations
tab, you can track

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.630
and see the status
of the invitations

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:42.320
that you've sent
to the students.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.340
You can also resend
invitations, if needed.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.230
To add and invite
individual students,

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.540
complete the following steps.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.240
Open the Coursera program for
the Associate Cloud Engineer

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.350
track, click on the
Invitations icon,

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:59.710
enter the individual's full
name and email address,

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:02.400
and click Send Invitation.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.209
The Import Members feature
enables you to add and invite

00:01:05.209 --> 00:01:07.280
multiple students at a time.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:11.120
To import members, start by
creating an invitee list.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.480
Create a spreadsheet with
column names exactly as shown--

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:18.290
full name, email, external ID.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:22.010
The values in the external
ID may be left blank.

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:25.500
Download the student
data as a CSV file.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.680
Here are the steps to import
students using your CSV invitee

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:29.910
list.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:33.670
From the Invitation tab,
click Import Members.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:37.520
Follow the instructions
in the Coursera dialog.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.500
When you complete the
Import Members step,

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.750
the students receive an
automatic invitation email

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.590
from Coursera.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.090
Your students are
now ready to start

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:48.510
learning on Coursera by opening
the Google Cloud Edu invitation

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:50.550
email with the
subject line, "You're

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.100
invited to learn on Coursera."

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.470
In the email, students
may click Join Program

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.380
to join the Associate
Cloud Engineer track.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.410
The student can then enroll in
the first course, Google Cloud

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:02.760
Platform Fundamentals--

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.150
Core Infrastructure.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.490
We have reviewed steps
for your account setup

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:11.030
in Coursera, student
invitations, and learning

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.040
progress monitoring.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.880
[MUSIC PLAYING]

